<title>UK: NWE oil products - mogas dips $1, others steady.</title>
<headline>NWE oil products - mogas dips $1, others steady.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE oil products were mixed on Thursday morning despite downward pressure from weaker Brent futures, traders said.</p>
<p>Gasoline lost $1 a tonne but gas oil and heavy fuel were little changed.</p>
<p>Barge and cargo prices for heating oil and diesel moved up by almost $2 a tonne in early business as July gas oil futures rose on pre-expiry short-covering and premiums strengthened.</p>
</text>
